## Description of the Change

According to https://github.com/gdg-tangier/vue-firestore/issues/50, `vue-firestore` seems to be unmaintained by now. This change removes it completely, replacing it simply by self-implementing the listeners with the corresponding Firestore functions.

Before (with vue-firestore):

```js
firestore () {
  return {
    items: {
      ref: this.$db.collection('items'),
      objects: true
    },
  }
}
```

After (without vue-firestore):

```js
data () {
  return {
    items: {}
  }
},
created () {
  onSnapshot(collection(this.$db, "items"), (snapshot) => {
    snapshot.docChanges().forEach((change) => {
      if (change.type === "added" || change.type === "modified") {
        this.$set(this.items, change.doc.id, change.doc.data())
      }
      if (change.type === "removed") {
        this.$delete(this.items, change.doc.id);
      }
    });
  });
}
```

This change also improved the initial loading of song and setlist lists on the dashboard.

## Benefits

One dependency less.

